{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/242032-do-you-use-the-wod-initiative-rules-as-written-why-or-why-not","id":242032,"title":"Do you use the WoD initiative rules as written? Why or why not?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-26T23:01:36-07:00","id":242032,"title":"Do you use the WoD initiative rules as written? Why or why not?","content":"You know, where everyone says what they are going to do in reverse initiative order before anything happens. I tried that once. I thought the increase in realism was more than negated by the awkwardness. Sure, everything happens faster when the turn gets going--but the extra step means combat takes longer overall. I dunno, maybe we just didn't do it long enough to really get used to it; it was only a four-session game. One argument in favor is that it rewards people for winning initiative. I say, go back to the original wound modifier scheme--0,-1,-2,-3,-4,-5, incapacitated, dead. That favors initiative winners pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T23:48:54-07:00","id":242052,"title":"","content":"When running the cWOD, I use the declaration phase. cWOD combat is fairly slow until you get significant system mastery anyway. I've found that the declaration phase can actually help the learning curve a lot in the long run.<br /> <br /> When I look at changing the initiative rules, I usually look to two things:<br /> <br /> 1) The DA Rev. multiple action rules. Not exactly a house rule, but I use it over the others as it makes multiple actions flow better in general.<br /> <br /> 2) Not re-rolling initiative each round unless the base scores are very tight or until there's a significant change in the flow of the fight. Keeping the init rolls rather than re-rolling them each round helps people get into a flow. They know who they declare after and act after giving them a predictable amount of time to prepare and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T09:52:31-07:00","id":242301,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/242032-do-you-use-the-wod-initiative-rules-as-written-why-or-why-not?p=242052#post242052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When running the cWOD, I use the declaration phase. cWOD combat is fairly slow until you get significant system mastery anyway. I've found that the declaration phase can actually help the learning curve a lot in the long run.<br /> <br /> When I look at changing the initiative rules, I usually look to two things:<br /> <br /> 1) The DA Rev. multiple action rules. Not exactly a house rule, but I use it over the others as it makes multiple actions flow better in general.<br /> <br /> 2) Not re-rolling initiative each round unless the base scores are very tight or until there's a significant change in the flow of the fight. Keeping the init rolls rather than re-rolling them each round helps people get into a flow. They know who they declare after and act after giving them a predictable amount of time to prepare and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>As this gentleman said <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T11:15:44-07:00","id":242342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryoga84</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/242032-do-you-use-the-wod-initiative-rules-as-written-why-or-why-not?p=242301#post242301\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As this gentleman said <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Thirded. And just to prove I'm not a spambot, here's a little more text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T20:56:25-07:00","id":244487,"title":"","content":"We've tried using the declaration phase, and it lasts maybe a round before we give up on it. We get why it's &quot;balanced&quot;, but it's just another list of things to remember, and takes more time to get through. Not only does the player have to remember what they were doing, but the ST does too. For our group, it just isn't worth it. Yes, that means that the last person to go gets to react last without penalty for making their decision of what to do until the end (and, that also means spending Rage/blood after everyone else has spent theirs), but the trade-off is just faster and easier for us.<br /> <br /> So, basically... the one who rolls highest declares their expenditure of Rage (for Werewolf), then declares their standard action, rolls, and finishes.<br /> Second-highest goes, and does the same... going down the line.<br /> Someone with an unspent action can spend their upcoming action to dodge/react if they'd like.<br /> The lowest initiative goes and declares their Rage and performs their actions in reaction to what everyone else has done. <br /> Then First Rage Actions go, starting with highest initiative, and down the line.<br /> <br /> Whether or not we all re-roll initiative, or keep our previous initiative is up to the ST and the group's thoughts at the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}